# Epic-level Human approval

<!-- cs: Schvalování na úrovni epiky -->

This rule **overrides** `rules/090-apm-orchestration.mdc` § B (the Human-gate column)
and `rules/070-project-management.mdc` where Phase R says "then Human reviews" and
where Phase E waits for Human approval of the plan before any Task starts
(FE.2 / FT.7). Report tiers by band stay as written in `090`.
<!-- cs: Toto pravidlo přebíjí sloupec Human gate v rules/090-apm-orchestration.mdc § B a místa v rules/070-project-management.mdc, kde Phase R říká „then Human reviews“ a kde Phase E čeká na schválení plánu člověkem, než začne jakýkoli task (FE.2 / FT.7). Úroveň reportu podle pásma zůstává podle 090. -->

## What stays

<!-- cs: Co zůstává -->

- Every Task still needs a Reviewer verdict. `REQUEST CHANGES` is fixed and
  re-reviewed. The three-round cap and band escalation in `000-model-policy.mdc`
  stay.
- A Task the Reviewer cannot approve, or a question only the Human can answer,
  stops the Epic. Ask one question (`005-decision-protocol.mdc`).
- Git commit and push still need an explicit trigger (`020-git.mdc`) or an
  explicit exception in the Human's message.

## What changes

<!-- cs: Co se mění -->

- Do not open a Human gate after a Task, in any band, when that Task has
  Reviewer `APPROVE` and no blocking question.
- Do not wait for FE.2 once the Human has asked to carry out the Epic.
- Finish every remaining Task of the Epic, then open one Human gate for the
  Epic (Phase ER, FER.2), using the briefing in `090` § C.
- The Human approves or rejects the Epic there. Per-task approval is not
  required.
